data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` into a `Span` of native-sized integers.** Both `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>` work:

```csharp
Span<nint>  nints  = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> nuints = stackalloc nuint[2];
```

On this 64-bit system, `nint.Size` is 8 bytes, so `nint.MaxValue` is `9223372036854775807` (same as `long.MaxValue`). On a 32-bit runtime it would be 4 bytes. No `unsafe` context is needed when assigning directly to a `Span<T>`.
